  "privacyPolicyHeading": "Privacy Policy for Karde",
  "privacyPolicyEffectiveDate": "Effective Date: September 2026",
  "privacySection1Title": "1. Local Storage Only",
  "privacySection1Body": "All your data, including card numbers, CVVs, and notes, is encrypted and stored locally on your device. We do not transmit, back up, or store your data on any external servers or cloud services. You have complete control over your data.",
  "privacySection2Title": "2. Encryption",
  "privacySection2Body": "Your data is secured using AES-256-GCM encryption. The encryption keys are securely generated and stored in your device's hardware-backed Keystore.",
  "privacySection3Title": "3. Authentication",
  "privacySection3Body": "To access your sensitive data, Karde requires local authentication via your device's Biometrics (Face ID/Fingerprint) or your custom Karde PIN. We do not have access to your PIN or biometric data.",
  "privacySection4Title": "4. Data Deletion",
  "privacySection4Body": "You can permanently delete all your data at any time using the \"Erase vault\" feature in Settings, or by uninstalling the application. Since no data is stored in the cloud, uninstallation results in permanent deletion of your vault.",
  "privacySection5Title": "5. Permissions",
  "privacySection5Body": "The app only requests permissions necessary for its core functionality, such as Biometric authentication. It does not request internet access, ensuring your data cannot be transmitted.",
  "privacySection6Title": "6. Changes to this Policy",
  "privacySection6Body": "We may update this policy occasionally. Any changes will be reflected in the app. By continuing to use the app, you agree to the updated policy.",
  "recoveryNoPinNote": "You chose to unlock Karde with your phone's own lock, so there is no Karde PIN to recover yet. Setting this up now means a way back in already exists if you ever add one.\n\nSeparately, and worth knowing: your items are encrypted with a key held in your phone's security chip. Changing your PIN, pattern, password or fingerprints is safe — your items stay readable. But if you turn your screen lock off completely, that key is destroyed and nothing here can bring your items back. An encrypted backup, from Settings, is the only thing that survives it.",
  "areYouSure": "Are you sure?",
  "confirm": "Confirm",
  "noScreenLockWarning": "This phone has no screen lock.\n\nKarde keeps your encryption key in the phone's security chip, and that chip will not hold a key unless the phone itself is locked. Until you set a PIN, pattern, password or fingerprint in your phone's settings, Karde cannot save or open any items.\n\nYou can finish setting up now, then add a screen lock and come back.",
