  "privacySection7Title": "7. Keep Your Screen Lock",
  "privacySection7Body": "Karde's encryption key lives in your phone's security chip, and it exists only while your phone has a screen lock. Changing your PIN, pattern, password or fingerprints is safe — your saved items stay readable. But if you turn your screen lock off completely, that key is destroyed and your items can no longer be opened by anyone, including us. An encrypted backup is the only thing that survives it, so make one before removing your screen lock.",
